#====================================================================
# DRAFT-gtk-3.24.38-broadway-ohos - Broadway build and no-display consumer validation
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-gtk-3.24.38-broadway-ohos
trigger_tool:           meson|ninja|gtk|python3
phase:                  configure|build|testing
error_signature:        broadway|X11|Wayland|HMDFS|shebang|libffi.so.8|GtkWindow

severity:               2
category:               meson|gtk|broadway|ohos-filesystem
match_keywords:         gtk, GTK+, Broadway, X11, Wayland, HMDFS, glib-compile-resources, GtkWindow
title:                  Build GTK 3.24 with Broadway and validate consumers without a display

root_cause:             The base OHOS runner has neither X11/Wayland nor the prerequisites required by the upstream GTK GUI tests. Ambient GLib tools can load an incompatible device-global libffi ABI, while pinned compiled tools copied from a Conan cache require HarmonyOS self-signing before execution.
verification_cmd:       conan create archives/g/gtk/3.24.38 --build=missing; require the signed GtkWindow type probe and R34 destructive dependency test to pass.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            broadway-headless-consumer-probe
rec_description:         Use the gtk Conan slug, enable Broadway, overwrite generated pkg-config tool variables with signed private copies of pinned compiled GLib tools, pair them with dependency library paths, and run a no-display consumer probe.
rec_command:             -Dx11_backend=false -Dwayland_backend=false -Dbroadway_backend=true
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                conan-recipe|portability-patch|test-package

forbid_1_pattern:         claim upstream GUI tests passed without display fixture
forbid_1_reason:          Display, input, theme, and upstream harness prerequisites are absent in the headless package gate.
forbid_1_consequence:    Test coverage is overstated and regressions may be hidden.

